---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Obedience Corp"
  description="Obedience Corp is researching organized diffusion: systems aimed at turning vague user intent into expected results with minimal intervention between input and outcome."
>
  <!-- ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
       Hero — company-level positioning for organized diffusion.
       ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
  <section class="hero">
    <div class="hero-inner">
      <div class="hero-head">
        <p class="mono-label hero-eyebrow">Organized diffusion</p>
        <h1 class="hero-h1">
          The executive<br />layer for AI.
        </h1>
      </div>

      <div class="hero-body">
        <p>
          AI can do more work than ever, and managing that work at scale is now the job. The executive layer lets you set the intent and direction, then keep the work legible and verifiable as it runs across agents, tools, and context.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="hero-ctas">
        <a href="#thesis" class="hero-cta hero-cta-primary">Read more <span aria-hidden="true">↓</span></a>
        <a href="/work" class="hero-cta">See the work <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
       Thesis section — continuation of the narrative, copy from the
       user's Landing Page Version. Honest about shipping status.
       ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
  <section id="thesis" class="thesis">
    <div class="thesis-inner">
      <p class="mono-label thesis-eyebrow">The Shift</p>

      <article class="thesis-body">
        <p class="thesis-lede">LLMs model language. Diffusion models resolve visual noise. <strong>Organized diffusion models execution</strong>, turning ambiguous intent into structured work across agents, tools, context, workflows, and artifacts.</p>

        <h2>Today you’re the connective tissue</h2>
        <p>AI agent harnesses do real work. They call tools, build things, search the web, write code, manipulate files. What they can’t do is reach the final outcome on their own. They run a few steps, stop, and hand control back. You review, redirect, kick off another loop. The work happens in fragments, and you are the connective tissue between every fragment.</p>
        <p>The gap isn’t that AI can’t do the work. It’s that today’s systems can’t sustain themselves through it. They need you to supply the structure, the judgment, the next step, every time.</p>

        <h2>What changes with organized diffusion</h2>
        <p>A well-run company doesn’t work by the CEO talking to every person doing every task. It works because the systems and processes around them let competent people succeed in their roles without constant oversight and messages. The CEO supplies intent and strategy. The organization runs.</p>
        <p>We can build agentic harnesses today that can resemble that type of system by modeling the systems and processes we have in place at human organizations, but at scale we introduce many new points of failure and overload the user with information.</p>
        <p>At its core, organized diffusion standardizes the organization of the work being done so we can more easily abstract the work being done so the human can understand it, trust it and audit it. This has an additional benefit of compounding performance and autonomy increases through normal usage.</p>

        <h2>User-owned by design</h2>
        <p>Your data, your context, and your history belong to you. They should be portable by default, easy to inspect, and easy to move. You shouldn’t have to fight to export your own information or rebuild your setup every time a tool changes direction.</p>
        <p>And because your information stays yours, you stay free to use whatever AI models and tools serve you best. New tools should plug into your data, not lock you into someone else’s platform.</p>

        <h2>Why this matters</h2>
        <p>Throughout history, productive leverage has only been in the hands of a few people at the top. CEOs of large companies, politicians, heads of institutions. The modern world opens paths for individuals to reach those positions, but they still involve a lot of luck, a lot of work, and a lot of time.</p>
        <p>Problems in the world that required extreme amounts of human leverage to solve were gated by the cost of getting to the highest levels of society. If one person in the world knew how to solve a massive problem with huge societal impact, they would still have to spend decades proving themselves worthy of the human leverage required to solve it, and be extremely lucky.</p>
        <p>As AI continues to get more capable and cheaper, solving massive problems requiring extreme amounts of coordinated effort becomes affordable to a wider pool of people. But very few people in society have experience effectively managing and organizing effort at scale, and the systems of organizing our work that people are familiar with are designed for a world that no longer exists.</p>
        <p>When you build an AI orchestration system based around existing work management systems, the scaling ceiling is around the amount of work the human can imagine themselves doing if they had the human resources to do the work, and the scaling capacity of the system is limited by the user's ability to conceptualize the capability of the system.</p>
        <p>When the capabilities start to expand beyond what the user has a mental model to support, the interface and the user become the bottleneck. Imagine if you woke up tomorrow and your baseline productivity increased by 10x. Within a few weeks you'll be able to adjust to that new normal.</p>
        <p>Now imagine if you woke up tomorrow and your baseline increased 5,000x, or 100,000x. What would you do with that capacity? How would you reason about the work being done at that scale to even know that the system is working? If you're running a company, how do you manage people when everyone you hire has this same level of capacity?</p>
        <p>The barrier to this scale of capability is not training a better llm model. It is making everything produced by the AI legible and verifiable and useful at scale, without mentally overwhelming the human director. And that's what organized diffusion enables us to build.</p>

        <blockquote>
          <p>The people who control their information flow will outperform the people who let algorithms, apps, and prompts control their day.</p>
        </blockquote>

        <p class="founder-note-trigger">
          <button type="button" id="founder-note-open" class="founder-note-link">
            Founder's note <span aria-hidden="true">→</span>
          </button>
        </p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
       Founder's note — modal dialog. Triggered from the thesis section.
       Native <dialog> with ESC to close, click-outside to dismiss.
       ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
  <dialog id="founder-note" class="founder-note-dialog" aria-labelledby="founder-note-title">
    <div class="founder-note-content">
      <button
        type="button"
        id="founder-note-close"
        class="founder-note-close"
        aria-label="Close founder's note"
      >
        <span aria-hidden="true">×</span>
      </button>

      <p class="mono-label founder-note-eyebrow">Founder's note</p>
      <h2 id="founder-note-title" class="founder-note-title">Where I am today</h2>

      <div class="founder-note-body">
        <p>I've been working on this system as a solo founder since early 2025, and I've been dogfooding it since May 2025. I've built more with this system in the past year than every team I've been on in my 11 years working in software, both in breadth and depth. I am completely reliant on my system because there is no viable alternative that can handle the workload that's now become normal to me.</p>
        <p>What's missing now is packaging, positioning, and financing. Today I can use the system to build complex products and set up automated coding or research pipelines that require a level of specification and reliability that can't be done with other systems.</p>
        <p>If I'm able to secure investment, the focus will be on productization, marketing, and demonstrations. If that doesn't work, I'm going to use it internally as either an employee or contractor until the next layer is done.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </dialog>

  <!-- ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
       Contact section — form copied verbatim from the previous
       src/pages/contact.astro (which is deleted in Task 8).
       ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
  <section id="contact" class="contact">
    <div class="contact-inner">
      <h2 class="contact-h2">Contact</h2>
      <p class="contact-intro">
        Reach out for early access to Obedience, a demo of Festival, investment, or partnership. Tell us what you're after.
      </p>

      <form
        id="contact-form"
        action="https://formspree.io/f/xgopdrej"
        method="POST"
        class="contact-form"
      >
        <input type="text" name="_gotcha" style="display:none" tabindex="-1" autocomplete="off" />

        <div class="form-field">
          <label for="name" class="mono-label">Name</label>
          <input type="text" id="name" name="name" required placeholder="Your name" />
        </div>

        <div class="form-field">
          <label for="email" class="mono-label">Email</label>
          <input type="email" id="email" name="email" required placeholder="you@example.com" />
        </div>

        <div class="form-field">
          <label for="message" class="mono-label">Message</label>
          <textarea id="message" name="message" required rows="5" placeholder="Tell us what you're interested in..."></textarea>
        </div>

        <button type="submit" class="submit-btn mono-label">
          Send message <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span>
        </button>

        <p id="form-status" class="form-status"></p>
      </form>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .hero {
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-rule);
    min-height: 100vh;
    min-height: 100svh;
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
  }

  .hero-inner {
    flex: 1;
    width: 100%;
    padding: clamp(3rem, 6vh, 5rem) clamp(1.25rem, 3vw, 3.5rem);
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    column-gap: clamp(2rem, 5vw, 5rem);
    row-gap: clamp(2rem, 4vh, 3rem);
  }

  @media (min-width: 960px) {
    .hero-inner {
      grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1.15fr) minmax(0, 1fr);
      align-items: end;
    }
    .hero-head { grid-column: 1 / 2; }
    .hero-body { grid-column: 2 / 3; margin: 0; }
    .hero-ctas { grid-column: 1 / -1; }
  }

  .hero-eyebrow {
    display: block;
    margin: 0 0 1.1rem;
    color: var(--color-ink-muted);
  }

  .hero-h1 {
    font-family: var(--font-serif);
    font-weight: 400;
    font-size: clamp(2.25rem, 9vw, 10rem);
    line-height: 1;
    letter-spacing: -0.028em;
    color: var(--color-ink-primary);
    margin: 0;
  }

  .hero-lede {
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
    font-weight: 400;
    font-size: clamp(1.0625rem, 1.5vw, 1.25rem);
    line-height: 1.45;
    color: var(--color-ink-muted);
    max-width: 60ch;
    margin: 1.5rem 0 3rem;
  }

  .hero-body {
    max-width: 52ch;
    margin: 2rem 0 2.5rem;
  }

  .hero-body p {
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
    font-size: clamp(1.0625rem, 1.15vw, 1.25rem);
    line-height: 1.6;
    color: var(--color-ink-body);
    margin: 0 0 1.25em;
  }

  .hero-body p:last-child {
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }

  .hero-ctas {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 1rem;
    justify-content: center;
    margin-top: 1rem;
  }

  .hero-cta {
    position: relative;
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 0.65rem;
    padding: 1.15rem 2.25rem;
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
    font-size: 1.0625rem;
    font-weight: 500;
    letter-spacing: -0.01em;
    color: var(--color-ink-primary);
    background: transparent;
    border: 1px solid var(--color-ink-primary);
    border-radius: 999px;
    transition: background-color 200ms ease, color 200ms ease,
      transform 200ms ease, box-shadow 200ms ease;
    will-change: transform;
  }

  .hero-cta > span {
    display: inline-block;
    transition: transform 220ms cubic-bezier(0.22, 1, 0.36, 1);
  }

  .hero-cta:hover {
    background: var(--color-ink-primary);
    color: var(--color-bg-primary);
    transform: translateY(-2px);
    box-shadow: 0 10px 24px -12px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.55);
  }

  .hero-cta:active {
    transform: translateY(0);
  }

  .hero-cta:focus-visible {
    outline: 2px solid var(--color-ink-primary);
    outline-offset: 3px;
  }

  /* Secondary "See the work →" — arrow slides right on hover */
  .hero-cta:not(.hero-cta-primary):hover > span {
    transform: translateX(4px);
  }

  .hero-cta-primary {
    background: var(--color-ink-primary);
    color: var(--color-bg-primary);
  }

  .hero-cta-primary:hover {
    background: transparent;
    color: var(--color-ink-primary);
  }

  /* Primary "Read more ↓" — arrow nudges down on hover */
  .hero-cta-primary:hover > span {
    transform: translateY(3px);
  }


  /* ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
     Thesis section
     ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── */
  .thesis {
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-rule);
  }

  .thesis-lede {
    font-family: var(--font-serif);
    font-size: clamp(1.25rem, 2vw, 1.6rem);
    line-height: 1.4;
    letter-spacing: -0.01em;
    color: var(--color-ink-primary);
    margin: 0 0 2.75rem;
  }

  .thesis-inner {
    max-width: 68ch;
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: clamp(4rem, 9vh, 7rem) clamp(1.25rem, 3vw, 3.5rem);
  }

  .thesis-eyebrow {
    display: block;
    margin-bottom: 2rem;
    color: var(--color-ink-muted);
  }

  .thesis-body {
    font-family: var(--font-serif);
    font-size: 1.0625rem;
    line-height: 1.75;
    color: var(--color-ink-body);
    max-width: 64ch;
  }

  .thesis-body > p {
    margin: 0 0 1.5em;
  }

  .thesis-body h2 {
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
    font-weight: 500;
    font-size: clamp(1.125rem, 1.75vw, 1.375rem);
    letter-spacing: -0.005em;
    color: var(--color-ink-primary);
    margin: 3rem 0 1rem;
  }

  .thesis-body ul {
    list-style: none;
    padding: 0;
    margin: 0 0 1.75em;
  }

  .thesis-body ul li {
    position: relative;
    padding-left: 1.75em;
    margin-bottom: 0.25em;
  }

  .thesis-body ul li::before {
    content: "·";
    position: absolute;
    left: 0.25em;
    color: var(--color-ink-muted);
  }

  .thesis-body strong {
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--color-ink-primary);
  }

  .thesis-body blockquote {
    margin: 3rem 0 0;
    padding: 2rem 0;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--color-rule);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-rule);
    font-size: clamp(1.25rem, 2vw, 1.5rem);
    font-style: italic;
    line-height: 1.4;
    color: var(--color-ink-primary);
    text-align: center;
  }

  .thesis-body blockquote p {
    margin: 0;
    max-width: 32ch;
    margin-left: auto;
    margin-right: auto;
  }

  /* ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
     Contact section
     ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── */
  .contact-inner {
    max-width: 52ch;
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: clamp(4rem, 9vh, 7rem) clamp(1.25rem, 3vw, 3.5rem);
  }

  .contact-h2 {
    font-family: var(--font-serif);
    font-weight: 400;
    font-size: clamp(1.75rem, 3.5vw, 2.5rem);
    line-height: 1.1;
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
    color: var(--color-ink-primary);
    margin: 0 0 1rem;
  }

  .contact-intro {
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
    font-size: 1.0625rem;
    line-height: 1.55;
    color: var(--color-ink-muted);
    max-width: 48ch;
    margin: 0 0 clamp(2rem, 4vh, 3rem);
  }

  .contact-form {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 1.75rem;
  }

  .form-field label {
    display: block;
    margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
  }

  .form-field input,
  .form-field textarea {
    width: 100%;
    background: transparent;
    border: none;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-rule);
    padding: 0.65rem 0;
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
    font-size: 1.0625rem;
    color: var(--color-ink-primary);
    outline: none;
    transition: border-color 150ms ease;
    resize: none;
  }

  .form-field input::placeholder,
  .form-field textarea::placeholder {
    color: var(--color-ink-muted);
  }

  .form-field input:focus,
  .form-field textarea:focus {
    border-bottom-color: var(--color-ink-primary);
  }

  .submit-btn {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 0.5rem;
    align-self: flex-start;
    margin-top: 0.5rem;
    padding: 0.65rem 0;
    border: none;
    background: transparent;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-ink-primary);
    color: var(--color-ink-primary);
    cursor: pointer;
    transition: opacity 150ms ease;
  }

  .submit-btn:hover {
    opacity: 0.6;
  }

  .form-status {
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
    font-size: 0.875rem;
    min-height: 1.5em;
    margin: 0;
  }

  .form-status[data-state="ok"] {
    color: var(--color-ink-primary);
  }

  .form-status[data-state="err"] {
    color: #b84a3d;
  }

  /* ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
     Founder's note — trigger + modal dialog
     ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── */
  .founder-note-trigger {
    margin: 2.5rem 0 0;
    text-align: center;
  }

  .founder-note-link {
    background: transparent;
    border: none;
    padding: 0.5rem 0;
    color: var(--color-ink-muted);
    cursor: pointer;
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 0.5rem;
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.8125rem;
    font-weight: 500;
    letter-spacing: 0.14em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-ink-muted);
    transition: color 150ms ease, border-color 150ms ease;
  }

  .founder-note-link:hover,
  .founder-note-link:focus-visible {
    color: var(--color-ink-primary);
    border-bottom-color: var(--color-ink-primary);
    outline: none;
  }

  .founder-note-link > span {
    display: inline-block;
    transition: transform 220ms cubic-bezier(0.22, 1, 0.36, 1);
  }

  .founder-note-link:hover > span,
  .founder-note-link:focus-visible > span {
    transform: translateX(3px);
  }

  .founder-note-dialog {
    border: none;
    padding: 0;
    background: transparent;
    color: var(--color-ink-body);
    max-width: min(56ch, calc(100vw - 2rem));
    width: 100%;
    margin: auto;
  }

  .founder-note-dialog::backdrop {
    background: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.55);
    backdrop-filter: blur(2px);
  }

  .founder-note-dialog[open] {
    animation: founder-note-fade-in 180ms ease-out;
  }

  .founder-note-dialog[open]::backdrop {
    animation: founder-note-backdrop-in 180ms ease-out;
  }

  @keyframes founder-note-fade-in {
    from { opacity: 0; transform: translateY(8px); }
    to   { opacity: 1; transform: translateY(0); }
  }

  @keyframes founder-note-backdrop-in {
    from { opacity: 0; }
    to   { opacity: 1; }
  }

  .founder-note-content {
    position: relative;
    background: var(--color-bg-primary);
    border: 1px solid var(--color-rule);
    padding: clamp(1.75rem, 4vw, 2.75rem) clamp(1.5rem, 4vw, 2.75rem);
  }

  .founder-note-close {
    position: absolute;
    top: 0.85rem;
    right: 0.85rem;
    background: transparent;
    border: none;
    color: var(--color-ink-muted);
    font-size: 1.5rem;
    line-height: 1;
    width: 2rem;
    height: 2rem;
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    cursor: pointer;
    border-radius: 999px;
    transition: color 150ms ease, background-color 150ms ease;
  }

  .founder-note-close:hover,
  .founder-note-close:focus-visible {
    color: var(--color-ink-primary);
    background: var(--color-rule);
    outline: none;
  }

  .founder-note-eyebrow {
    display: block;
    margin: 0 0 0.5rem;
    color: var(--color-ink-muted);
  }

  .founder-note-title {
    font-family: var(--font-serif);
    font-weight: 400;
    font-size: clamp(1.5rem, 3vw, 2rem);
    line-height: 1.15;
    letter-spacing: -0.012em;
    color: var(--color-ink-primary);
    margin: 0 0 1.5rem;
  }

  .founder-note-body {
    font-family: var(--font-serif);
    font-size: 1rem;
    line-height: 1.7;
    color: var(--color-ink-body);
  }

  .founder-note-body > p {
    margin: 0 0 1.25em;
  }

  .founder-note-body > p:last-child {
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }
</style>

<script>
  // Founder's note modal — open/close wiring for the native <dialog>.
  const founderDialog = document.getElementById('founder-note') as HTMLDialogElement | null;
  const founderOpen = document.getElementById('founder-note-open');
  const founderClose = document.getElementById('founder-note-close');

  founderOpen?.addEventListener('click', () => founderDialog?.showModal());
  founderClose?.addEventListener('click', () => founderDialog?.close());

  // Click outside the content panel (i.e. on the backdrop) closes the dialog.
  founderDialog?.addEventListener('click', (e) => {
    if (e.target === founderDialog) founderDialog.close();
  });

  const form = document.getElementById('contact-form') as HTMLFormElement | null;
  const status = document.getElementById('form-status') as HTMLElement | null;

  form?.addEventListener('submit', async (e) => {
    e.preventDefault();
    const data = new FormData(form);

    try {
      const res = await fetch(form.action, {
        method: 'POST',
        body: data,
        headers: { Accept: 'application/json' },
      });

      if (status) {
        if (res.ok) {
          status.textContent = "Message sent. We'll be in touch.";
          status.dataset.state = 'ok';
          form.reset();
        } else {
          status.textContent = 'Something went wrong. Please try again.';
          status.dataset.state = 'err';
        }
      }
    } catch {
      if (status) {
        status.textContent = 'Network error. Please try again.';
        status.dataset.state = 'err';
      }
    }
  });
</script>
